WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.120
Look, Brian. Those are our motorcycles, David says.

00:08.340 --> 00:11.780
David and Brian are at Heathrow Airport

00:12.020 --> 00:16.760
in London. They are motorcycle racers from Enfield,

00:17.300 --> 00:28.110
a small town in England. They usually

00:28.160 --> 00:33.350
go to Brazil. Racers from many countries are

00:33.400 --> 00:37.090
going there too. They are all going to

00:37.140 --> 00:44.260
race across the Amazon jungle. Brian is reading a newspaper.

00:46.260 --> 00:51.290
Listen to this, David, he says. There's a

00:51.340 --> 00:55.750
problem in the Amazon. The Indians are very

00:55.800 --> 00:59.760
angry because miners are going into the jungle.

01:01.280 --> 01:05.880
The miners are taking their homes. But David

01:06.360 --> 01:10.270
isn't listening to Brian. The race is going

01:10.320 --> 01:16.240
to be good, he says. Yes, and difficult,

01:16.600 --> 01:16.900
David.

01:19.580 --> 01:23.200
Two days later, the racers are in Brasilia.

01:24.080 --> 01:29.570
Brian and David are there too. A lot of people come and

01:29.620 --> 01:34.830
watch. It is a beautiful sunny morning. There

01:34.880 --> 01:39.220
is a lot of noise. People are talking to the racers.

01:40.180 --> 01:45.610
Photographers are taking pictures. The race is going

01:45.660 --> 01:49.080
to start, a young man says. Listen.

01:50.140 --> 01:55.130
Good morning, a man says. This is the

01:55.180 --> 02:01.410
start of the Amazon rally. 42 people are going to race

02:01.460 --> 02:06.640
from here to Manaus. Are you okay, Brian?

02:07.540 --> 02:15.260
David asks. No, Brian answers. I've got a problem. Look,

02:16.140 --> 02:19.560
oil is leaking from the engine of my motorcycle.

02:21.580 --> 02:25.640
Where's that glue for oil leaks? Brian asks.

02:26.780 --> 02:29.120
The racers are putting on their helmets.

02:30.040 --> 02:35.450
Here, try this, David says. He gives Brian

02:35.500 --> 02:39.700
some glue. Brian puts some glue on his engine,

02:40.160 --> 02:44.460
but it comes out very slowly. Quickly, Brian,

02:45.160 --> 02:48.860
the race is going to start, David says.

02:50.140 --> 02:55.000
But oil is leaking from Brian's engine. Quickly,

02:55.600 --> 03:02.290
David says again. The oil stops. Brian puts on

03:02.340 --> 03:10.200
his helmet and gets on his motorcycle. The engines of the motorcycles make a lot of noise.

03:11.500 --> 03:16.380
The race is starting, David says. Let's go,

03:17.000 --> 03:20.940
Brian says. The Amazon rally starts.

03:22.160 --> 03:27.590
The first day is okay. The roads are

03:27.640 --> 03:32.560
good. The racers see many small towns and villages.

03:33.820 --> 03:36.800
People stand near the road and watch them.

03:38.220 --> 03:42.660
On the second day, the roads are not very good.

03:43.540 --> 03:49.580
Two Italians, Luigi and Enrico, are in first and second place.

03:50.860 --> 03:57.880
On the third day, the racers are in the jungle. The roads are very bad.

03:59.320 --> 04:02.250
The Brazilians are in first and second place

04:02.300 --> 04:08.170
now. Then, come Luigi and Enrico, David and

04:08.220 --> 04:10.880
Brian are behind the two Italians.

04:12.660 --> 04:16.280
The race always stops late in the afternoon.

04:17.580 --> 04:24.720
Those Brazilians are very good and they know the road, Brian says that evening.

04:26.680 --> 04:34.580
The Brazilians aren't a problem. The rain is our big problem. Look, David answers.

04:39.280 --> 04:44.170
Day four. This is our second day in

04:44.220 --> 04:49.330
the jungle. A difficult day. The rain never

04:49.380 --> 04:52.620
stops and the road is very bad.

04:53.620 --> 05:00.380
There are trees across the roads. Sometimes, we can't stay on our motorcycles.

05:01.980 --> 05:06.050
I am first in the race now and

05:06.100 --> 05:13.940
David is second. The two Italians are behind us. We are happy about that.

05:15.860 --> 05:23.710
It is seven o'clock now and it is very dark. The days are very hot

05:23.760 --> 05:27.880
in the jungle. But the nights are beautiful.

05:29.680 --> 05:34.800
David is in bed. I am going to bed, too.

05:38.080 --> 05:45.530
The race starts very early on the third day in the jungle. In the afternoon, Brian

05:45.580 --> 05:46.780
and David stop.

05:47.980 --> 05:55.450
The jungle is very beautiful, but they aren't looking at it. They are looking for the

05:55.500 --> 05:57.420
town of Una Una.

05:59.120 --> 06:04.470
Where are we now, Brian asks? I don't

06:04.520 --> 06:08.560
know. Is this the road to Una Una?

06:09.460 --> 06:12.560
I don't know, David says again.

06:13.960 --> 06:18.910
Where are the racers, Brian asks? Can you

06:18.960 --> 06:22.920
hear them? They stop their engines and listen.

06:23.720 --> 06:29.220
The jungle is quiet. Then they hear a noise.

06:30.300 --> 06:36.270
Listen, David, Brian says. What is it? David

06:36.320 --> 06:40.940
asks. It isn't a motorcycle, Brian answers.

06:42.400 --> 06:48.120
Suddenly they see some men. They are walking to Brian and David.

06:49.260 --> 06:54.190
Look at those men, David. Brian says. Who

06:54.240 --> 06:59.700
are they? David asks. They aren't racers, David.

07:00.660 --> 07:02.420
They are Indians.

07:04.600 --> 07:11.880
The Indians come and talk to Brian and David, but the two young men can't understand them.

07:13.180 --> 07:18.520
These Indians are very angry, Brian. But why?

07:19.440 --> 07:23.100
I don't know. I can't understand them.

07:24.260 --> 07:30.290
We've got a problem, Brian, David says. The

07:30.340 --> 07:33.860
Indians take the two young men to an Indian village.

07:34.640 --> 07:38.570
A woman with blue eyes comes and talks

07:38.620 --> 07:44.840
to Brian and David. Her name's Astrid and she's German.

07:46.620 --> 07:50.860
She lives in the jungle because she's working there with the Indians.

07:52.340 --> 08:00.300
Who are you? The woman asks. I'm Brian and this is my friend David.

08:01.380 --> 08:07.450
Why are the Indians angry? David asks. Are

08:07.500 --> 08:12.140
you miners? The miners want this place.

08:13.120 --> 08:16.350
Sometimes they come here and they kill the

08:16.400 --> 08:23.310
Indians, Astrid says. We aren't miners. We are motorcycle

08:23.360 --> 08:27.750
racers, David says. We want to go to

08:27.800 --> 08:34.280
Una Una. Astrid talks to Maoni, the Indian chief.

08:35.720 --> 08:41.700
Maoni listens and talks to his men. They aren't angry now.

08:44.120 --> 08:51.060
The miners are coming to the village, Astrid says. Chief Maoni knows that

08:52.020 --> 08:58.820
they're going to kill his men. Let's get the police Astrid, Brian says.

08:59.800 --> 09:05.030
How? There's no time. I can go to

09:05.080 --> 09:09.600
Una Una. There's a police station there, Brian says.

09:10.720 --> 09:13.610
But you don't know the road to Una

09:13.660 --> 09:19.420
Una, David says. Astrid and Chief Maoni talk again.

09:21.500 --> 09:24.910
Kawak is going to go to Una Una

09:24.960 --> 09:32.600
with you tomorrow. He's Chief Maoni's son and he knows the road, Astrid says.

09:36.940 --> 09:43.200
At seven o'clock in the morning, Brian and Kawak get on Brian's motorcycle.

09:44.480 --> 09:49.430
Kawak isn't very happy. He doesn't know about

09:49.480 --> 09:53.500
motorcycles. The Indians watch them.

09:54.700 --> 09:58.930
Brian starts the engine and Kawak gets off

09:58.980 --> 10:03.220
the motorcycle quickly. The Indians run to the trees.

10:05.220 --> 10:10.640
Astrid talks to Kawak. Then he gets on the motorcycle again.

10:11.300 --> 10:17.600
The Indians watch from the trees. Brian starts the engine again.

10:19.140 --> 10:26.320
Go, David says. Brian and Kawak take the road to Una Una.

10:28.220 --> 10:35.840
It is difficult in the jungle, but Brian is a good racer and Kawak knows the road.

10:36.480 --> 10:40.040
He knows every river and tree in the jungle.

10:42.080 --> 10:49.080
Early in the afternoon, they come to a big river. Brian looks in his roadbook.

10:50.100 --> 10:55.800
They are near Una Una now. Then Brian looks at the engine.

10:56.760 --> 11:01.370
Oh no! Oil is leaking from the engine

11:01.420 --> 11:05.720
again, he thinks. He stops the motorcycle.

11:07.360 --> 11:11.720
I haven't got any glue. Where's David's glue?

11:12.520 --> 11:12.820
He thinks.

11:14.000 --> 11:16.920
This time I've got a big problem.

11:18.880 --> 11:26.100
Kawak looks at the oil. Then he walks to a tree and takes a green fruit.

11:27.280 --> 11:29.840
He puts the fruit on the hot engine.

11:31.140 --> 11:32.740
The leak stops.

11:34.160 --> 11:39.440
That's very good, Brian says. Thank you, Kawak.

11:40.220 --> 11:41.200
Let's go!

11:42.500 --> 11:48.500
They start to drive again. The oil often leaks from the engine,

11:49.340 --> 11:57.020
but Kawak stops it with the green fruit every time. They arrive in Una Una in the evening.

11:58.460 --> 12:02.020
They meet Captain Silver at the police station,

12:02.700 --> 12:04.440
and Brian talks to him.

12:05.720 --> 12:12.280
The miners are coming, Captain. They're going to kill the Indians, Brian says.

12:13.660 --> 12:18.100
You're right, young man. We don't have much time.

12:19.120 --> 12:26.700
Captain Silver talks to a policeman. Let's go to the Indian village. I want 20 men.

12:27.620 --> 12:27.980
Quickly.

12:29.920 --> 12:33.620
They get to the Indian village late in the afternoon.

12:34.840 --> 12:38.740
Let's wait for the miners, Captain Silver says.

12:39.640 --> 12:41.080
Go behind the trees.

12:42.820 --> 12:47.240
It's night again. They are all waiting for the miners.

12:49.140 --> 12:53.140
Look, Captain Silver says. They're coming.

12:54.860 --> 12:59.980
The miners are coming from the jungle. They're moving very quietly.

13:01.040 --> 13:06.740
There are a lot of miners in the village now. They are looking for the Indians.

13:08.360 --> 13:13.720
The village is quiet. Then Captain Silver says,

13:14.720 --> 13:20.230
this is Captain Silver. Don't move! The miners

13:20.280 --> 13:22.960
run, and the Indians run too.

13:23.640 --> 13:30.000
They make a lot of noise. Two miners find David and catch him.

13:31.180 --> 13:35.770
They're going to kill me, David thinks. But

13:35.820 --> 13:40.680
then two policemen run to him. Stop, they say.

13:41.520 --> 13:42.250
We are policemen.

13:42.300 --> 13:49.150
In the morning, Chief Maune and his people

13:49.200 --> 13:54.020
are very happy. A lot of Indians are dancing.

13:55.840 --> 14:00.090
Chief Maune has two beautiful necklaces in his

14:00.140 --> 14:05.080
hands. He smiles and gives a red necklace to David.

14:06.640 --> 14:11.750
Jaguarri, he says. He's giving you an Indian

14:11.800 --> 14:17.610
name, Astrid says. Jaguarri is a small jaguar.

14:19.180 --> 14:23.800
Then Chief Maune gives a black necklace to Brian.

14:25.200 --> 14:31.560
Manui, he says. Quick runner, Astrid says.

14:32.980 --> 14:39.690
Brian gives his helmet to Kowak. Champion, he

14:39.740 --> 14:42.320
says. They all smile.

14:44.800 --> 14:49.080
Captain Silver takes Brian and David to Manaus.

14:49.980 --> 14:54.000
The races are there. There are photographers too.

14:54.880 --> 14:58.850
They are taking pictures of the champions, Luigi

14:58.900 --> 15:05.720
and Enrico, the two Italians. Brian, David, hello.

15:06.880 --> 15:11.930
Enrico says, Look, we are the champions, Luigi

15:11.980 --> 15:16.520
says. Congratulations, Brian and David say.

15:17.320 --> 15:22.460
Are you okay? Enrico asks. Now we are,

15:23.140 --> 15:28.310
Brian says. Brian and David's talk to Enrico

15:28.360 --> 15:31.620
and Luigi about the Indians and the miners.

15:32.860 --> 15:39.270
Your champions too, Luigi says. Yes, they're champions

15:39.320 --> 15:43.820
of a very important race, Captain Silver says.

15:45.620 --> 15:49.140
Brian and David look at their Indian necklaces.

15:50.200 --> 15:54.760
Congratulations, Manui, David says to his friend.

15:56.380 --> 16:00.140
Congratulations, Jaguarri, Brian says.
